{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChABwBhTDwdRPxrM8U4KK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the bug in `app.py`. `slugify` now lowercases the title, splits it on whitespace and joins the words with hyphens:\n\n```python\nreturn \"-\".join(title.lower().split())\n```\n\nSplitting on whitespace ignores spaces at the start and end and treats a run of spaces as one break, so you don't get empty parts. `slugify(\"Hello World\")` now gives `hello-world`, and `\"  Many   spaces here \"` gives `many-spaces-here`. The test in `test_app.py` passes, and I didn't change that file.\n\nThis also turns tabs and newlines into hyphens, not just spaces. Punctuation is still left in the slug as it was before, since the issue didn't ask about it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":262,"cache_read_input_tokens":7880,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":262},"output_tokens":232,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c4475c58-1b01-462e-ab51-78c309636bee","uuid":"876acb53-c990-48b2-a857-06d4295d02f7","timestamp":"2026-11-18T09:53:07.132Z","request_id":"req_011ChABwBa1LiQmoi2ZKjdQq"}
